Hi Alex — quick tech notes and a paste of minimal pseudo-code you can drop into your service.

1) Streaming + structured event (pseudo):
---
// subscribe to stream for UX tokens
client.on('token', t => renderToken(t));

// server emits final structured event once tool-calls complete
client.on('structured_result', obj => postToWorker(obj));
---

We emit a separate final event (structured_result) from the SDK when the model returns the validated JSON/tool-call. This avoids partial-JSON headaches and lets your worker rely on a single canonical payload.

2) Embeddings -> reranker (pseudo):
---
// compute embeddings for query
qVec = sdk.embeddings.encode(query);
// fetch candidate doc vectors, compute similarity, then call model for reranking with context and candidate list
ranked = reranker.rank(query, candidates, {model: 'rdrw-rerank-v1'});
---

3) Token budgeting: include token_count in the envelope metadata and emit warnings if a request approaches configured limits.

I attached a tiny example folder (rsp-schema-examples.json included by Marissa). If you want, I can open a quick screen-share tomorrow to walk the code.

